 signs: \n - Blood pressure: 119/83 mmHg\n - Heart rate: 72 bpm\n - Respiratory rate: 16 breaths per minute\n - Temperature: 98.6°F\n - Weight: 151 lbs\n- General: Alert and oriented, in no acute distress\n- Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs, rubs, or gallops\n- Respiratory: Clear to auscultation bilaterally\n- Musculoskeletal: Tenderness noted in the area, no deformities\n- Skin: Erythematous patches and pustules on the face consistent with rosacea\n\n**Hospital Course:**\nMs. Lowe’s hospital course was uneventful. She was managed conservatively with medications for her musculoskeletal injury and continued on he"
